<title>UK: Iran earned $100 billion from oil sales in 1989-93.</title>
<headline>Iran earned $100 billion from oil sales in 1989-93.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iran earned $97 billion from crude oil exports and $3.5 billion from oil product sales from 1989 to 1993, the OPEC official news agency reported an Iranian petroleum ministry official as saying.</p>
<p>The country's petroleum export earnings in the year ended March 19, 1996 were $16 billion, the Iranian state news agency reported recently.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8145</p>
</text>
